1
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:21,000
From above the world of Cars

2
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Planes is a animation, family, adventure film directed by Klay Hall.

3
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Dusty is a cropdusting plane who dreams of competing in a famous aerial race.

4
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
The problem?

5
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:21,000
He is hopelessly afraid of heights.

6
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:36,000
With the support of his mentor Skipper and a host of new
friends, Dusty sets off to make his dreams come true.

7
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Dusty Crophopper (voice), played by Dane Cook.

8
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
El Chupacabra (voice), played by Carlos Alazraqui.

9
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Bravo (voice), played by Val Kilmer.

10
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Rochelle (voice), played by Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

11
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Chug (voice), played by Brad Garrett.

12
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Dottie (voice), played by Teri Hatcher.

13
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:21,000
Planes is a 2013 American animated sports comedy film produced by
Disneytoon Studios, and a spin-off of Pixar's Cars franchise.

14
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
The film stars the voices of Dane Cook, Stacy Keach, Priyanka Chopra,  Teri Hatcher, Brad Garrett, Julia
Louis-Dreyfus, Roger Craig Smith, John Cleese, Carlos Alazraqui, Anthony Edwards, Sinbad, and Val Kilmer.

15
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
In the film, Dusty Crophopper, a crop duster plane in the town of Propwash Junction, wants to complete the Wings Around
the Globe racing challenge, despite his fear of heights, with the help of naval aviator Skipper Riley.

16
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film was directed by Klay Hall and written by Jeffrey M.

17
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:21,000
In developing a concept created by John Lasseter, the writers made a conscious effort to avoid remaking Cars in a
new setting, while reusing Keach and Danny Mann's characters from the Cars Toons short "Air Mater".

18
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The production team conducted research by interviewing several
pilots of plane types that were included in the movie.

19
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
Jon Cryer was initially announced as the voice of
Dusty, before being replaced by Cook.

20
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Despite dropping out, Cryer received credit on the
film for "additional story material".

21
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
The musical score was composed by Mark Mancina, while Prana Studios
provided work on visual effects, animation and compositing.

22
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Planes premiered on August 2, 2013, at EAA AirVenture
Oshkosh, a gathering of aviation enthusiasts.

23
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
It was initially intended to be released as a direct-to-video film, but
was instead released theatrically on August 9, 2013.

24
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It received generally negative reviews from critics and
grossed $240 million against a $50 million budget.

25
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
A sequel, Planes: Fire & Rescue, was released in 2014.

26
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:36,000
The film explores themes of countryside, sports,
competition, training, crop duster.

27
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:51,000
The tone is lighthearted.
